ModuleLinker resolves `requires` against a process-global registry of
compiler-provided builtin modules (BuiltinModules.all(), which lives in the
runtime module Cardinal does not take). This makes that universe an argument
instead, so a Cardinal context supplies the modules its runners contribute and
two contexts with different vocabularies can coexist in one JVM.

The no-argument overloads are kept and delegate with an empty universe, so
every existing call site behaves as before.

